      "Private rituals (rituais de fundamento) are closed to non-initiates and constitute Candomblé's esoteric core: preparing assentamentos (shrines containing each orixá's sacred stones, herbs, tools, and offerings); conducting ebós; performing obrigações (periodic ritual renewals at 1, 3, 7, 14, and 21 years post-initiation); and managing the terreiro's fundamentos (spiritual foundations, including the axé plantado—ritually 'planted' spiritual force at the terreiro's founding). These practices involve complex choreographies of prayers, songs, gestures, and offerings known only to senior initiates. Knowledge circulates vertically through initiatory lineages, with each generation learning from the previous under oaths of secrecy.",
